#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:5
msgid "Migrating to PEP 639 License Expressions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:7
msgid ""
"Starting with setuptools v77.0.0, the ``project.license`` field accepts an "
"`SPDX license expression <https://spdx.org/licenses/>`_ as defined in :pep:"
"`639`. The previous TOML-table forms (``license = {text = \"...\"}`` and "
"``license = {file = \"...\"}``) are deprecated and will be removed in a "
"future version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:13
msgid "This guide helps you migrate your project's license configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:17
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:20
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:22
msgid ""
"The ``project.license`` field in ``pyproject.toml`` historically accepted a "
"TOML table, either with a ``text`` key holding a license description or a "
"``file`` key pointing at a license file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:26
msgid ""
"# Old format (deprecated)\n"
"license = {text = \"Apache-2.0\"}\n"
"# or\n"
"license = {file = \"LICENSE\"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:33
msgid ""
"Starting with setuptools v77.0.0, ``project.license`` is instead a string "
"containing an SPDX license expression, and the files themselves are declared "
"separately via ``project.license-files``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:37
msgid ""
"# New format (PEP 639)\n"
"license = \"Apache-2.0\"\n"
"license-files = [\"LICENSE\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:43
msgid ""
"The SPDX expression format is standardized and supports composing licenses "
"(for example ``\"Apache-2.0 OR MIT\"`` or ``\"GPL-3.0-only WITH Classpath-"
"exception-2.0\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:48
msgid "Migrating your configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:51
msgid "Replace a ``{text = ...}`` license"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:53
msgid ""
"If the ``text`` value was already a recognized license identifier, use it "
"directly as an SPDX expression:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:56
msgid ""
"# Before\n"
"license = {text = \"MIT\"}\n"
"\n"
"# After\n"
"license = \"MIT\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:64
msgid ""
"If the ``text`` was free-form prose rather than a license identifier, "
"express the license as an SPDX expression and ship the full text as a "
"license file (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:69
msgid "Replace a ``{file = ...}`` license"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:71
msgid ""
"Point ``license`` at the SPDX expression and list the file under ``license-"
"files``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:74
msgid ""
"# Before\n"
"license = {file = \"LICENSE\"}\n"
"\n"
"# After\n"
"license = \"Apache-2.0\"\n"
"license-files = [\"LICENSE\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:83
msgid ""
"``license-files`` accepts glob patterns, so multiple files (for example a "
"project license plus third-party notices) can be included:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:86
msgid "license-files = [\"LICENSE*\", \"NOTICE\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:91
msgid "Replace license classifiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:93
msgid ""
"The ``License :: ...`` trove classifiers are also deprecated in favor of "
"SPDX expressions. Drop them from ``classifiers`` and record the license in "
"``license`` instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:97
msgid ""
"# Before\n"
"classifiers = [\"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\"]\n"
"\n"
"# After\n"
"license = \"MIT\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:106
msgid "Requiring a compatible setuptools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:108
msgid ""
"SPDX expressions and the ``license-files`` field are understood by "
"**setuptools v77.0.0 and later**. This is a *build-time* requirement on "
"setuptools itself; it is independent of the Python versions your project "
"supports at runtime (``requires-python``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:113
msgid ""
"Most build frontends (such as :pypi:`build` and :pypi:`pip`) build in an "
"isolated environment and install the latest setuptools by default, so simply "
"declaring the minimum in ``[build-system].requires`` is usually enough:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:117
msgid ""
"[build-system]\n"
"requires = [\"setuptools>=77\"]\n"
"build-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n"
"\n"
"[project]\n"
"name = \"my_package\"\n"
"license = \"Apache-2.0\"\n"
"license-files = [\"LICENSE\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userguide/license_migration.rst:128
msgid ""
"If you need to keep supporting builds with an older setuptools, retain the "
"old TOML-table form (it continues to work, with a deprecation warning) until "
"you can require setuptools v77+."
msgstr ""

